  "notes": "Nonprofit foundation (GAAP, net assets) supporting Grand Island Public Schools; manifest entity_type is school district (Miscellaneous Districts) but it is not a district, so entity_type 'other'. No governmental/proprietary fund split: all lines recorded as governmental; net assets treated as fund balance. Statements are two-page spreads (left pages 1, 3, 7 = General..Jack Martin columns; right pages 2, 4, 8 = Marshall..Total All Accounts); all statement figures from the 2025 Total All Accounts column. Receipts = revenues without donor restrictions (printed total 1,392,421) plus donor-restricted revenue lines; 'Net assets released from restrictions' (953,625 / (953,625)) nets to zero and is left out. Unclaimed scholarships and Other income without donor restrictions are '-' (not recorded). No single printed total of all revenues: reported receipts total computed. Identity: 11,490,112 + 2,772,380 - 1,991,255 = 12,271,237 (ties). Beginning cash 3,307,854 and ending cash 3,525,677 from the Statement of Cash Flows (p8); ending_cash is the 'Cash' line of the Statement of Financial Position (CDs 122,256 and investments separate). proprietary null (no proprietary funds; cash flow statement shows net operating 406,538 and investing (188,715), p8). Balance sheet: Statement of Financial Position, scholarships/grants payable as other liabilities (current and long-term). Detail: Statement of Functional Expenses 2025 (p5), one line per expense-type column (Program, General and Administrative, Fundraising), ties to 1,492,530 / 265,534 / 233,191; p6 is the 2024 comparative (not used). Read pages 1-8 of 8"
